; An item's description (item.<id>.desc): the paragraph in its details dialog
; (a right-click). A new item needs one, or its dialog has no paragraph.
item.rune_fire.desc=A stone tablet cut with Kenaz, the rune of fire. Commit it to memory and the symbol is yours to cast; the tablet is spent in the learning.
item.rune_earth.desc=A stone tablet cut with Berkano, the rune of earth. Commit it to memory and the symbol is yours to cast; the tablet is spent in the learning.
item.rune_air.desc=A stone tablet cut with Ansuz, the rune of air. Commit it to memory and the symbol is yours to cast; the tablet is spent in the learning.
item.rune_water.desc=A stone tablet cut with Laguz, the rune of water. Commit it to memory and the symbol is yours to cast; the tablet is spent in the learning.
item.rune_project.desc=A tablet cut with Tiwaz, the rune of projection, the form that sends a spell flying at a foe. Memorizing it spends the tablet.
item.rune_protect.desc=A tablet cut with Algiz, the rune of protection, the form that wraps a spell around the party as a ward. Memorizing it spends the tablet.
item.rune_sight.desc=A tablet cut with Dagaz, the rune of sight, the form that turns a spell into a way of seeing. Memorizing it spends the tablet.
item.rune_multiple.desc=A tablet cut with Ingwaz, the rune of the many. It follows a form and multiplies it: more bolts, or a ward for the whole party. Memorizing it spends the tablet.
item.rune_explode.desc=A tablet cut with Hagalaz, the rune of hail. It follows a form and makes it burst: a bolt that explodes, or a ward that blasts all around. Memorizing it spends the tablet.
item.dagger.desc=A plain, well-balanced dagger. Quick in the hand, for stabbing and slashing.
item.khukri.desc=A heavy, forward-curved blade that bites deep with every chop.
item.flamebrand.desc=A khukri forged in a fire that never quite went out. Its blows burn.
item.frostbrand.desc=A blade that is always cold to the touch. Its cuts carry a freezing bite.
item.serrated_blade.desc=A saw-toothed blade that tears as it cuts, leaving wounds that bleed.
item.snake_dagger.desc=A wavy-bladed dagger, sinuous as a serpent and as quick.
item.french_dagger.desc=A long, slender dagger of foreign make, as good for a thrust as for a cut.
item.club.desc=A knotted length of hardwood. Slow to swing, but it lands hard.
item.leather_armor.desc=Hardened leather over chest and back. It turns a glancing blow without slowing you much.
item.padded_jack.desc=A quilted jacket of layered cloth. Light, and better than nothing against a blade.
item.brigandine.desc=Small steel plates riveted inside a cloth coat. Solid protection that still moves with you.
item.mail_hauberk.desc=A long shirt of riveted rings. Superb against a slash, heavy on the shoulders.
item.plate_cuirass.desc=A breastplate of shaped steel. Nothing turns a blow better, and nothing weighs more.
item.tunic.desc=A plain woollen tunic. Warm enough, but it will stop very little.
item.apple.desc=A crisp apple, a little bruised. It takes the edge off hunger and thirst alike.
item.bread.desc=A dense round of travelling bread. Filling, if dry.
item.waterskin.desc=A leather waterskin, full. Two good drinks.
item.torch_crude.desc=A rag-wrapped stick in an iron sleeve. It lights the way, but not for long.
item.torch_crude_lit.desc=A crude torch, burning. It will not last long; stowed it goes out, but set down it burns on where it lies.
item.torch.desc=A pitch-soaked torch on a wooden haft, good for a quarter of an hour of light.
item.torch_lit.desc=A torch, burning. It lights the party's way while it is held; stowed it goes out, but set down it burns on where it lies.
item.torch_fine.desc=A fine torch: an iron cup of pitch and tallow on a turned haft. It burns long and bright.
item.torch_fine_lit.desc=A fine torch, burning steadily. It lights the party's way while it is held; stowed it goes out, but set down it burns on where it lies.
item.torch_magic.desc=A fine torch worked with a quiet enchantment. Lit, it burns with a cold blue flame and lasts far longer than any pitch could.
item.torch_magic_lit.desc=A magical torch, burning blue. It lights the party's way for a long while; stowed it goes out, but set down it burns on where it lies.
item.torch_stub.desc=The charred end of a torch, burnt down to nothing. There is no light left in it.
item.waterskin_half.desc=A leather waterskin, half full. One good drink left.
item.waterskin_empty.desc=An empty leather waterskin. Fill it, and it will keep water for the road.
item.pebble.desc=A small, smooth stone, conjured from nothing. Good for a throw.
item.crypt_token.desc=A carved token, worn smooth by many hands. Its markings speak of a relic hidden somewhere below the crypt.
item.sunken_relic.desc=The relic the token spoke of, cold and heavier than it looks. Someone went to great lengths to hide it.
item.backpack.desc=A sturdy canvas pack with room for six things. Anything that fits in the hand fits in here.
item.ammo_pouch.desc=A stiff leather pouch made to hold ammunition, and nothing else.
item.medicine_pouch.desc=A small pouch for potions and remedies, lined to keep the bottles whole.
item.herb_pouch.desc=A soft pouch for gathered herbs and other ingredients.
item.herb.desc=A sprig of some bitter dungeon herb, worth keeping for whoever knows its use.
item.mushroom.desc=A pale mushroom from the damp dark. Better gathered than eaten raw.
item.iron_key.desc=A heavy iron key, dark with age. Somewhere a door is waiting for it.
item.rock.desc=A fist-sized lump of stone, heavy enough to hurt. Not much use in a pack, but it can be thrown.
item.fire_flask.desc=A stoppered clay flask, warm to the touch. Thrown, it shatters and bursts into flame - keep well back.
item.poison_flask.desc=A sealed flask of murky green vapour. Thrown, it shatters and a choking cloud creeps out from where it broke.
item.brass_key.desc=A small brass key, its teeth still sharp. It fits a lock somewhere in these halls.

