map.world.help.title=How the world's settings work
map.world.help.start=THE START CELL is where a party stands when a new game begins on the world map. It refuses impassable ground, because a party that cannot stand on its own start is a fault the check would report.
map.world.help.opening=WHERE THE GAME BEGINS is a different fact, and it lives in the manifest rather than in the world: a game may open inside a dungeon and never see the map until it climbs out. The party still has a world position either way — it is where it came in from.
map.world.help.areas=AN AREA overrides its terrain's danger over a rectangle. They may overlap, and where they do the LAST row wins, so a broad region is authored first and its exceptions carved out after it. That is why this is a list you can reorder rather than a sorted table.
map.world.help.doorways=A DOORWAY is a way in, not a dungeon: one dungeon may have several, a front gate and a back way that stands elsewhere on the map and lands elsewhere inside. Where you land belongs to the doorway; where you surface belongs to the exit stair you leave by.
