map.balance.help.title=How an attack's numbers work
map.balance.help.damage=damage is a multiplier. A swing's raw hit is (weapon damage + stat bonus) x skill scale, then x this: 0.8 lands 20% lighter, 1.3 lands 30% heavier. It scales with the weapon and the stats.
map.balance.help.accuracy=accuracy adds percentage points to the to-hit roll (base + DEX + skill, minus the defender's evasion, clamped 5-95%): +0.05 is five points more likely to land, -0.05 five points less.
map.balance.help.speed=speed multiplies the seconds between swings (the weapon's pace, shaved by DEX). Lower is faster: 0.8 swings a fifth quicker, 1.25 a quarter slower. A missed swing pays it too.
map.balance.help.stamina=stamina multiplies the swing's exertion cost (stamina_swing + stamina_weight x the weapon's kg). An empty bar leaves the attacker EXHAUSTED - weaker, slower swings - until it recovers.
map.balance.help.notes=The type column is the damage type the defender resists the hit as (the skeleton shrugs pierce, fears bash). These rows are global: edit stab and every stabbing weapon changes together. Per-weapon character comes from the weapon's own damage, speed and stats fields.
